        {
          "node_type": "item",
          "title": "FAPI / RAR (RFC 9396)",
          "description": ", SD-JWT (RFC 9901), Transaction Tokens and agent extension (implementations: Tokenetes, kontxt, keycloak-tts), Identity and Authorization Chaining Across Domains, Txn-Token Chaining Profile, OAuth Actor Profile, Attenuating Agent Tokens (monotonically-attenuating JWT delegation chains with tool-level argument constraints; offline derivation, no issuer contact), Human Delegation Provenance (HDP) (Ed25519-signed append-only hop chain binding human authorization to agent sessions), DAAP (runtime identity for dynamically-spawned agents), CB4A (credential broker architecture: PDP/CDP separation, SPIFFE identity, DPoP binding, proxy/mint/wrap delivery patterns), ID-JAG (Identity Assertion JWT Authorization Grant — agent provider signs assertion for cross-domain identity hop; see auth.md for an agent onboarding profile composing ID-JAG with discovery, account linking, client establishment, and delegated access in one click; analysis), CAEP and SSF, Deferred Token Response (async approval-gated token issuance — agent polls while human reviews), Transaction Authorization Challenge (agent presents to AS for human/authority approval, receives RAR-scoped token as evidence; agent untrusted to modify challenge), Condition-Bound Keys (hardware-rooted non-exfiltratable key that exists only while actor + platform + local policy conditions hold), JWT Authorization Grants in MCP, Token Exchange in MCP, AWS Bedrock AgentCore OBO token exchange (RFC 8693 / RFC 7523 OBO for agents, also Microsoft EntraID OBO sample)",
          "children": [],
